"""Third round (4 Nov 2026) for ED IIIa, ED IIIb and Ebla, after ShG's review of the worksheet (rows 2-37, evidence
rows 2-67). New works: Yoffee 2005 (Myths of the Archaic State), Bramanti 2020 (ch. 2 in Mynářová & Alivernini eds.,
printed page = PDF page + 7), Archi 2015 (Ebla and its Archives, SANER 7; printed page = PDF page - 25),
Benati & Bonechi 2020 (ch. 3 in the same Prague volume; ShG's copy is the final manuscript .docx, so the citation gives
the section; printed pages to be added), Steinkeller 1993 on northern Babylonia, Kleinerman 2021 (ch. 2 in Vita ed.,
History of the Akkadian Language), Notizia & Visicato 2016 (CUSAS 33).
New fields (scoring v2, see 85b_build_scores_v2.py):
  basis  = what the statement rests on (ShG's confidence rubric): 'assertion' (no evidence cited, or a reconstruction),
           'fragmentary' (few, fragmentary or extrapolated texts or finds), 'documented' (texts, finds or scientific results
           support it, incl. a comparative or negative example), 'substantial' (large numbers of texts or finds relative to
           what survives from that place and period).
  genre  = the Sitz im Leben of the underlying sources: admin, legal, letters, royal (inscriptions, propaganda), literary,
           lexical, archaeology, mixed.
  archive= the archive(s) the evidence comes from, as named in 84_archive_inventory.py.
  region = sub-entity, when the statement is about one part of the period's world (e.g. 'north (Kiš)', 'south').
Scores may be half points (1.5 = 'between 1 and 2') when the statement itself is in between."""
